Rast wrote:
...
> Now is probably not the appropriate time to make major changes in the 
> scoring system.  (But the ridiculous behavior of ties should be fixed.)

You mean that each person tied for a particular spot receives the full 
point value for that spot?

That doesn't seem ridiculous to me; yes, it's not exactly what most 
sports do, but it seems appropriate here.  While sporting rules are 
usually aimed at establishing a clear single winner, that's never made a 
lot of sense to me: adding irrelevant comparisons just to prevent having 
a shared victory just seems silly.  And it can't be that I watched too 
much Sesame Street as a child, since I grew up without a television.  ;-)

If (to take the most obvious example) you were tied with someone else 
for the Best Behaved trophy, the fact that another has achieved the same 
number of successful conducts in no way lessens _your_ achievement.  Why 
should it be valued less just because two folks managed to achieve the 
same number?

If marvin, eidolos2 and sawtooth all manage to stay tied in the Best of 
13 for the whole month, I'd argue they all deserve _at least_ to have 
the full value of that trophy credited to their clans; that's an 
_amazing_ achievement.

Anyway, at the end of the month it's _extremely_ unlikely that a 
significant number of trophies will be ties.  Looking through the 
archives, it seems that we've only had two instances of a tie at the 
tournament's end: once with Most Ascensions, and once with Best Behaved 
Ascension.

